Mendukung pembuatan laporan rutin serta pemeliharaan dashboard interaktif untuk memudahkan pemantauan performa departemen secara real-time.

Product Manager (Content Platform / Data Platform)

Responsibilities

1.Responsible for the planning and design of the company’s content distribution platform (including content review, task distribution, and data analytics);

2.Design and optimize core business workflows (Creator Upload → Review → Publish → Data Collection → Settlement);

3.Produce high-quality product documentation (PRD), process flows, and prototypes;

4.Work closely with engineering teams (frontend & backend) to ensure efficient implementation of product requirements;

5.Track project progress, coordinate resources, and ensure timely delivery;

6.Continuously optimize product features and user experience based on data insights;

7.Participate in business strategy design (commission structure, creator management, content strategy, etc.);

Requirements

1.At least 2 years of experience as a product manager in internet companies; platform product experience is preferred;

2.Experience across the full product lifecycle (requirement analysis → design → launch → iteration);

3.Proficient in prototyping tools (such as Axure, Figma, etc.);

4.Strong logical thinking, capable of independently designing complex business workflows;

5.Excellent communication and coordination skills, able to drive cross-functional execution;

6.Basic data analysis skills, able to optimize products based on data;

7.Strong sense of ownership, execution ability, and adaptability in a fast-paced environment;

Core Competencies (Key Focus )

1.Ability to design complex workflow systems (e.g., review workflows, task flows, state transitions)

2.Strong understanding of platform-based business models (e.g., creator management, content distribution, data attribution)

3.Data-driven mindset (able to design metrics such as clicks, conversions, GMV, etc.)

4.Strong execution capability (not only writing documents, but also ensuring product delivery)

Preferred Qualifications

1.Experience in content platforms (short video / MCN);

2.Experience in e-commerce or commission-based systems;

3.Familiarity with TikTok or other social media platforms;

4.Experience with data platforms or BI systems;

Key Responsibilities:

Quality Management System (QMS) & Compliance

Own and optimize factory Quality Management System (QMS) in line with lSO 9001 IS0 14001,1S0 45001,and company standards;

Translate customer requirements into product specifications (FG, semi-FG) and ensure regulatory & company compliance;

Manage specifcation lifecycle: version control, periodical reviews, and cross-functional update communication, maintain version history for alignment and feasibility;

Ensure compliance with GMP, product traceability, pest & hygiene management calibration and validation reguirements;

Manage deviation, non-conformance;

Optimize specifications via batch performance analysis to enhance consistency and customer satisfaction

Product & Process Quality Assurance

Oversee quality control plans (QCP), product release, and shop floor quality standards;

Monitor process stability, SPC, Cp/Gpk, defect PPM, rework, scrap, and cost;

Lead quality risk management including Process FMEA and implement preventive controls;

Ensure proper storage, FEFO, labelling, segregation for materials and products;

Product Specification & Data Governance

Own accuracy and compliance of all specifications for FG, semi-FG;

Maintain product data integrity across SAP, EHS, R&D, and factory systems;

Coordinate with Supply Chain, WH for compliant labelling and on-time release;

Quality lmprovement & Process Capability

Lead continuous improvement (Cl) projects to reduce defects, scrap, rework, and retests;

Conduct periodic process capability reviews and drive improvement actions;

Build quality dashboards, conduct trend analysis, and deliver data-driven improvementrecommendations;

Quality Performance & Reporting

Define, monitor, and report quality KPls;

Lead daily to monthly quality review meetings and provide management with insights and action plans;

Drive quality culture, training, and awareness on SPC, Six Sigma, RCA, CAPA, and mistake-proofing;

Team Leadership & Management

Lead, coach, and develop the quality team to meet performance objectives;

Collaborate cross-functionally with Production, Technology, Engineering, and Supply Chain;

Align quality objectives with company strategy and ensure timely delivery of all projects and action plans;

Requirements:

Bachelor's degree in Science, Applied Science, Engineering, or related field.

Minimum 3 years of quality management experience in tobacco, FMCG, or high speed manufacturing.

Thorough knowledge of HNB/tobacco reconstituted sheet processes and quality standards is a plus.

Proficiency in Quality tools, and risk management.

Experience in product specification management and system data governance (SAP, MES etc.).

Language Requirements:

Fluent in English & Bahasa

Chinese is a plus

Responsibilities :

